From 5b1e840fbf3de2882df10d3b019378de18c2602e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:00:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libipa: camera_sensor_helper: Add ov05c10

Without an entry for ov05c10 the software ISP used by the simple
pipeline handler cannot convert analogue gain codes and logs:

  IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for ov05c10

IPASoftSimple::configure() then uses the raw V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN
code as if it were a gain multiplier, so AGC runs over a nominal gain
range of 16-248 with a step of 1.0 instead of 1-15.5 with a step of
0.145, and its controller is mis-scaled over the whole range.

The OmniVision OV05C10 is used on Intel IPU6 and IPU7 laptops. Its
driver advertises analogue gain codes 0x10 to 0xf8 on
V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN and documents both endpoints:

  #define MAX_ANA_GAIN	0xf8  // 15.5x
  #define MIN_ANA_GAIN	0x10  // 1x

0x10 / 16 == 1 and 0xf8 / 16 == 15.5, so the gain is linear with a
divisor of 16. This is the same shape as the other OmniVision sensors
in this file, which use divisors of 128 or 256.

The sensor outputs 10-bit Bayer data and applies a fixed 0x40 (64 LSB)
black level pedestal. Measured on dark frames captured at minimum
exposure and minimum gain, the median is exactly 64 in each of the
four Bayer channels, with no per-channel difference. That scales to
4096 at the 16-bit width expected by blackLevel().

Tested on an HP EliteBook X G2i (Intel Panther Lake, IPU7), where the
OV05C10 is the only camera and is driven by the simple pipeline
handler. With the helper present the software ISP reports
"gain 1-15.5 (0.145)" in place of "gain 16-248 (1)".

Signed-off-by: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 9457d62b3..5379d087d 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -677,6 +677,18 @@ public:
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov01a10", CameraSensorHelperOv01a10)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperOv05c10 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperOv05c10()
+	{
+		/* From dark frame measurement: 0x40 at 10bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 16 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov05c10", CameraSensorHelperOv05c10)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperOv08x40 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
-- 
2.55.0

